; compiler-compare-fraction-const (#1186) - a comparison with a constant
; with a fraction gives the same boolean in every destination (Byte, Word,
; Long, Quick, Float): two such constants, one against a Quick or Float
; variable in both orders, negated, of each size, and whole-number
; constants of each size.  The fix of #1177 fetches the right operand of
; a comparison without a wanted type (a constant with a fraction is a
; Float there), but the left operand under a Byte destination went
; through the byte sizing of constants, which cuts the constant to a
; whole number: rb.b=(1.5=1.5) compared 1 with 1.5 (0), (1.5<1.5) was -1.
vq.q=1.5 : vf.f=2.5 : vb.b=1
